  "body": "Set against a spectacular backdrop of Rangitoto Island and the sparkling Hauraki Gulf, this substantial 776sqm freehold property presents an exciting opportunity in sought-after Mairangi Bay.\r\n\r\nThe existing character home offers a versatile layout, with four bedrooms plus a study (or fifth bedroom), alongside multiple living areas to suit families of all ages and stages. There is excellent connection to the outdoors on both sides of the home, with seamless flow to the north-facing lawn and established gardens creating a sun-soaked setting for family living and entertaining. A double internal-access garage and extensive off-street parking provide ample space for multiple vehicles, a motorhome, boats and trailers.\r\n\r\nYet it is the land, outlook and underlying potential that make this property particularly compelling. Whether you’re looking to enjoy it as is, add value with cosmetic upgrades and a pool, undertake a substantial renovation, create a new architectural home or investigate future development possibilities (subject to Council approval), this is a property that deserves serious consideration.\r\n\r\nEnjoy a sought-after coastal position just a few minutes’ stroll from the beach and Mairangi Bay Village, with its local cafés and shops. Excellent schools, including Rangitoto College, are also within walking distance.\r\n\r\nWith its substantial freehold site and exceptional outlook, this is an opportunity to secure a foothold in one of Mairangi Bay’s sought-after coastal locations. The question is how you choose to make it your own.\r\n\r\nTo be sold by way of Tender (unless sold prior), 4.00pm, Thursday 5th November 2026, 4 Bute Road, Browns Bay, Auckland\r\n\r\nAll agents welcome - conjunctions invited. \r\nMarketed by: Jo Harwood and Tara Menzies",
